{"parentUuid":"8de88b69-e0f1-4610-b34e-a32f6ffe625a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-09","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/large-downloads","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_01IYGtvkCAGZup8bub34llV7","content":"\nreal\t0m12.611s\nuser\t0m0.022s\nsys\t0m0.088s\nexit 0\n-rw-r--r-- 1 dev dev 59648809 Sep 18 10:25 /tmp/book.pdf"}]},"uuid":"d4d4e3d6-d27f-487c-9ae4-0edb5f35055f","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:22:41.000Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d4d4e3d6-d27f-487c-9ae4-0edb5f35055f","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/home/dev/quillmark","sessionId":"insight-09","version":"2.0.17","gitBranch":"fix/large-downloads","type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_01JWCeYfdqNOB6JSekmcsYcL","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Reproduced. At 1 MB/s the transfer is cut at exactly 30 seconds with 17 MB of 59 MB written; at full speed it finishes in 12.6 s. The 30 seconds is the server's WriteTimeout.\n\nIn Go, http.Server.WriteTimeout is not a timeout per write. It sets one deadline for the whole response, starting when the request headers have been read, so it covers the render (about 11 s for this book) and the entire body transfer. A large book to a slow client simply runs out of time, the server closes the connection, and the client keeps a truncated, unreadable PDF.\n\nRaising WriteTimeout for the whole server would also loosen it for every other route. Since Go 1.20, a handler can move its own deadline with http.NewResponseController(w).SetWriteDeadline, so the download route can get more time and the rest keeps 30 s."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":711,"output_tokens":532}},"uuid":"bd7ed4c5-a701-4de4-8c7f-d396ed39485d","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:22:50.000Z","requestId":"req_011CN04pu1gDHlLlXfQQucKh"}
